        "original_id": "3a244dd2-bf15-57d8-a77b-d4f6d5395312",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Larry Hagman, Nagisa Oshima\n- Roles: actor, director, producer, screenwriter\n- Works: Dallas, I Dream of Jeannie, In the Realm of the Senses, Merry Christmas, Mr. Lawrence\n- Topics: film, television\n\nFacts:\n- Larry Hagman was born on September 21, 1931, and he was an American film and television actor, director, and producer.\n- Nagisa Oshima was born on March 31, 1932, and he was a Japanese film director and screenwriter.\n- Larry Hagman was best known for playing Major Anthony \"Tony\" Nelson in the 1960s sitcom \"I Dream of Jeannie.\"\n- Nagisa Oshima directed \"In the Realm of the Senses\" in 1976, a sexually explicit film set in 1930s Japan.\n- Larry Hagman was best known for playing J.R. Ewing in the 1980s primetime television soap opera \"Dallas.\"\n- Nagisa Oshima directed \"Merry Christmas, Mr. Lawrence\" in 1983, a film about Japanese World War II prisoners of war.\n- Larry Hagman died on November 23, 2012.\n- Nagisa Oshima died on January 15, 2013.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
